{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127028-ex-bale-hound-mentor","id":127028,"title":"Ex-Bale Hound mentor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-06T15:42:42-07:00","id":127028,"title":"Ex-Bale Hound mentor","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115874-wolves-of-hell-brainstorming-forsaken-inferno-game-possibly-idigam-chronicles\">In my planned <b>Werewolf</b> game</a> I put my newly hunted and First Changed PCs against Bale Hounds pack that rules the territory of small Swedish town and nearby villages. Maeljin servants are all representing Deadly Sins and they expelled one of them and replaced her for better werewolf on her place, especially, as she was having doubts and \u201cgone to soft\u201d. I think to make her mentor for PCs \u2013 after few months of \u201cbanishment\u201d she return to semi-normal Harmony ( I think about maybe 5 ), contacted with Forsaken Firstborn to return to the Tribe, and now she wants cold revenge on Bale Hounds, even if it's partially righteous one. She will hunt and \u201cmark\u201d the Wolf-Blooded people to awoke Wolf in them, so they could fight with Bale Hounds with her. She's a bit manipulative and really do anything to exact her fury \u2013 even become one and make more of new Forsaken.<br /> <br /> And here are question I want you help me answer for this game:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>In what Maeljin service she should be in her Bale Hounds times?</b> She really is manipulative, love \u201cbeing the wolf\u201d and hunting, and treat others like her toys often. I was thinking she should work for Carnala, but after reading about her servants I don't think she would gone for it \u2013 she isn't so much self-destructive. She love to \u201chave fun\u201d but don't want the all senseless violence. Or get caught for that mater. So what are your though and propositions on this?<br /> <br /> 2. <b>What Auspice she should have as mentor figure?</b> From my little knowledge of system, I can't decide. For me she could be First Changed under any moon, Any ideas here?<br /> <br /> 3. <b>What Tribe she should join after her return to Forsaken?</b> There was advised to me she should be Blood Talon after she want's to hunt on other werewolves, but I'm not sure here. I could see her also as Hunter in Darkness, for her fondness of \u201cpure wolf experience\u201d. But the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/houses-of-the-moon/\" target=\"_blank\">new Tribes spoiler</a> point they aren't for inter-werewolves hunts. What do you see on this?<br /> <br /> 4. Bonus question \u2013 <b>what would be great, twisted name for town in English?</b> I was thinking about something like Small Heaven, to contrast with all evils and sins being center of chronicle. Any ideas?<br /> <br /> And here is music video that, at least partially, helped me shape this character...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/PVzljDmoPVs\" data-code=\"PVzljDmoPVs\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/PVzljDmoPVs/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T16:47:56-07:00","id":127077,"title":"","content":"1) Go for the one that serves Greed. I can't remember the name, and I might have watched one too many Game of Thrones episodes, but there are a number of greedy people who are excellent, excellent manipulators. Greed is destructive as well \u2014 there's a phenomenon among real wolves where they'll go into a fenced-in flock of sheep to kill something for food, but then end up killing a chunk of the flock.<br /> <br /> 2) Gishtahus are sociopaths by nature, prone to violence and whose entire Auspice blessing revolves around being a martyring cannibal. Some manage to control their impulses, but I can see one being a <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheSvengali\" target=\"_blank\">Svengali</a> to another wolf. You'll want to look them up in <i>Signs of the Moon</i>.<br /> <br /> 3) Here's the issue: it's very, very likely your wolf will remain a Ghost Wolf, and not even the Lunes themselves will tolerate her. There's a section in <i>Blasphemies</i> that compares rehabilitating a Bale Hound as equivalent to trying to let Jeffrey Dahmer be forgiven and let into normal society again \u2014 Bale Hounds. Are. Depraved. They can just as evil and horrific as the the acts of oWoD's Black Spiral Dancers, though the Dancers are a tad more off the evil end than they are. You're likely to have your character be the target of a number of <i>siskur-dah</i> rather than be accepted.<br /> <br /> That being said, something that might be interesting is a pack of ex-Bale Hounds who take care of each other and are trying to climb back up the Harmony slope.<br /> <br /> 4) Twisted town name? What about <b>Fell</b>? According to the <i>Encyclopedia of Arda</i>'s &quot;<a href=\"http://www.glyphweb.com/arda/words.html\" target=\"_blank\">Old and Rare Words</a>&quot; section, &quot;fell&quot; has three meanings:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1 merciless, terrifying </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">2 animal's hide</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">3 moorland hill</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Things like &quot;Eden&quot; or &quot;Paradise&quot; or &quot;Small Heaven&quot; are really, really unsubtle. It can add to the, &quot;Oh, *BLEEP*,&quot; factor of a scene if you give foreshadowing/etymology to a place that doesn't kick in until later. It's a well-used horror trope that the quiet little town has a cutesy little name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 05-06-2014, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T00:39:58-07:00","id":127301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127028-ex-bale-hound-mentor?p=127077#post127077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Go for the one that serves Greed. I can't remember the name, and I might have watched one too many Game of Thrones episodes, but there are a number of greedy people who are excellent, excellent manipulators. Greed is destructive as well \u2014 there's a phenomenon among real wolves where they'll go into a fenced-in flock of sheep to kill something for food, but then end up killing a chunk of the flock.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got almost flashed out Greed Hound - mayor of town, Elodoth, bargin for &quot;favors&quot; with his cultist. But I don't think she would fit as Hound of Greed. Yes, she is manipulative, but it's more &quot;I like to play with peoples feelings&quot; way. Really, I'm only having problem with servants of Carnala being so much easy to caught in the act. If Hounds of Asmodai can restrain they Rage and forge it in something truly wicked, why would those working for Lady of Lust must be so deprived you are first to be hunt for?<br /> <br /> I smell the setting hack is in need here...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127028-ex-bale-hound-mentor?p=127077#post127077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Gishtahus are sociopaths by nature, prone to violence and whose entire Auspice blessing revolves around being a martyring cannibal. Some manage to control their impulses, but I can see one being a <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheSvengali\" target=\"_blank\">Svengali</a> to another wolf. You'll want to look them up in <i>Signs of the Moon</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't find them on quick look. Could you put page number I could see them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127028-ex-bale-hound-mentor?p=127077#post127077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Here's the issue: it's very, very likely your wolf will remain a Ghost Wolf, and not even the Lunes themselves will tolerate her. There's a section in <i>Blasphemies</i> that compares rehabilitating a Bale Hound as equivalent to trying to let Jeffrey Dahmer be forgiven and let into normal society again \u2014 Bale Hounds. Are. Depraved. They can just as evil and horrific as the the acts of oWoD's Black Spiral Dancers, though the Dancers are a tad more off the evil end than they are. You're likely to have your character be the target of a number of <i>siskur-dah</i> rather than be accepted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get this, and read this section in <b>Blasphemies</b>. But to this game to work, she must be able to teach PCs the normal Forsaken culture and help them communicate with Firstoborns. She could be Ghost Wolf, but she need to be able to make PCs &quot;proper&quot; protagonists of game and that players couldn't smell &quot;it's a trap!&quot; thing to whole chronicle to work. Could she teach about Father Wolf, Mother Luna and help them get Lunes even if they would despise her?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127028-ex-bale-hound-mentor?p=127077#post127077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, something that might be interesting is a pack of ex-Bale Hounds who take care of each other and are trying to climb back up the Harmony slope.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think she could work again with her once cult brothers and sisters, but if PCs would do this, I think it could be nice final of this game. But for now let it be great idea for you to use. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-07-2014, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T16:07:32-07:00","id":127799,"title":"","content":"She can make them proper protagonists of the games by being a ghost wolf and INTRODUCING them to other uratha, without her necessarily meeting said uratha.<br /> <br /> Remember with the forsaken the first born KNOW you, baring the protection of soulless wolf which she will not have. I know Fenris would never take her in.<br /> <br /> edit: you should also consider running the bale hounds as the 9th tribe.<br /> <br /> edit edit: Members of the Forsaken will inherently not trust her. Individual Uratha may, but the whole community? They'd likely execute her. Should make her character incredibly redemptive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 05-07-2014, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T22:34:08-07:00","id":127987,"title":"","content":"Next question: <b>What should be good Deed Name for her? </b>I have still problem with this convetion on to which to look for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127028-ex-bale-hound-mentor?p=127799#post127799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She can make them proper protagonists of the games by being a ghost wolf and INTRODUCING them to other uratha, without her necessarily meeting said uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Idea was to limit NPCs in this game - there are Bale Hounds pack, there is ex-Bale Hound mentor, and there are PCs. Finito. I didn't wanted to introduce all Uratha society, only make very local game. The PCs are shut down with Bale Hounds and human cultists in one valley. In <b>Mage</b> I would just left players some Grimoires teaching basics of Order dogmats and few Rotes. No need for other mages, because basics are there. I can't make the same in <b>Werewolf</b>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127028-ex-bale-hound-mentor?p=127799#post127799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember with the forsaken the first born KNOW you, baring the protection of soulless wolf which she will not have. I know Fenris would never take her in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand now she couldn't get back to any Tribe, at least she would totally redeem herself. But couldn't she - I don't know - summon Firstborn on behalf of PCs, so <b>they</b> could join the Tribe? I'm very fond of the setting hack were <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/121131-using-the-firstborn?p=122010#post122010\">Firstborn partake more active role in lives of Uratha</a> and sometimes teaching them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127028-ex-bale-hound-mentor?p=127799#post127799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you should also consider running the bale hounds as the 9th tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm considering this, or general &quot;the cult that is inflitrating Forsakens&quot;. &quot;Nineth Tribe&quot; way gets very interesting finale for chronicle - after fighting with Bale Hounds, PCs comes to nearest metropoly and then expose Bale Hounds to all Forsaken. And great werewolf hunts begins... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127028-ex-bale-hound-mentor?p=127799#post127799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Members of the Forsaken will inherently not trust her. Individual Uratha may, but the whole community? They'd likely execute her. Should make her character incredibly redemptive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want other Forsaken in this game. I want her to teach basics to PCs and make players fitting to work with classical society later on. I really wants to make this game small in scope, maybe even Tier Zero game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-08-2014, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T15:41:04-07:00","id":128573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127028-ex-bale-hound-mentor?p=127077#post127077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) Twisted town name? What about <b>Fell</b>? According to the <i>Encyclopedia of Arda</i>'s &quot;<a href=\"http://www.glyphweb.com/arda/words.html\" target=\"_blank\">Old and Rare Words</a>&quot; section, &quot;fell&quot; has three meanings:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Things like &quot;Eden&quot; or &quot;Paradise&quot; or &quot;Small Heaven&quot; are really, really unsubtle. It can add to the, &quot;Oh, *BLEEP*,&quot; factor of a scene if you give foreshadowing/etymology to a place that doesn't kick in until later. It's a well-used horror trope that the quiet little town has a cutesy little name.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Fell</b> has very interesting conotations in Swedish:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_gt-baf-table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_tr\"><td colspan=\"4\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Fell-<span style=\"color:#777777\"><i>rzeczownik</i></span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <div align=\"right\"> <br /> </div></td> <td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\">avverkning</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> fell, disforestation</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <div align=\"right\"> <br /> </div></td> <td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\">f\u00e4ll</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> fell, pelt, skin rug</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <div align=\"right\"> <br /> </div></td> <td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\">skinn</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> leather, skin, hide, Fur, pelt, fell</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <div align=\"right\"> <br /> </div></td> <td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\">hud</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> skin, hide, integument, pelt, fell</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <div align=\"right\"> <br /> </div></td> <td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\">berg</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> mountain, Rock, mount, hill, outcrop, fell</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_tr\"><td colspan=\"4\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Fell-<span style=\"color:#777777\"><i>czasownik</i></span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <div align=\"right\"> <br /> </div></td> <td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\">f\u00e4lla</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> precipitate, drop, shed, fell, couch, deposit</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <div align=\"right\"> <br /> </div></td> <td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\">avverka</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> fell, cut, log, accomplish, do, make</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <div align=\"right\"> <br /> </div></td> <td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\">hugga ner</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> cut down, fell</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_tr\"><td colspan=\"4\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Fell-<span style=\"color:#777777\"><i>przymiotnik</i></span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <div align=\"right\"> <br /> </div></td> <td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\">grym</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> cruel, ferocious, savage, atrocious, vicious, fell</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <div align=\"right\"> <br /> </div></td> <td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\">hemsk</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> terrible, awful, uncanny, weird, gruesome, fell</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <div align=\"right\"> <br /> </div></td> <td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\">d\u00f6dlig</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"> fatal, lethal, deadly, mortal, deathly, fell</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> It has very good meanings for many <b>Werewolf </b>themes - I like it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T17:33:50-07:00","id":128638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127028-ex-bale-hound-mentor?p=128573#post128573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has very good meanings for many <b>Werewolf </b>themes - I like it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And just in case one of your players picks up on that: make it so that, if you do use that name, it's because of a feature of the town. It's a good name for something built in a marshy area, or something was used/is still used a lot in the fur trade and clothesmaking market. That's often how towns IRL get their names \u2014 something important to the area.<br /> <br /> As for the deed name, why not <b>Cunning Tongue</b>? Subtle, shows she's good at talking, could be taken the wrong way if you have a dirty mind (if you're still making her a servant of Carnala). I'll even translate it for you, I just have to pull up my dictionary again. I also mentioned the Gishtahu auspice earlier; you can find it on page 193 or 194 of <i>Signs of the Moon</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T17:52:08-07:00","id":128653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127028-ex-bale-hound-mentor?p=128638#post128638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And just in case one of your players picks up on that: make it so that, if you do use that name, it's because of a feature of the town. It's a good name for something built in a marshy area, or something was used/is still used a lot in the fur trade and clothesmaking market. That's often how towns IRL get their names \u2014 something important to the area..</div> </div> </div> </div>Game is set in mountains valley, but wolves and bears fur trade post could be good one for this, yes? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127028-ex-bale-hound-mentor?p=128638#post128638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the deed name, why not <b>Cunning Tongue</b>? Subtle, shows she's good at talking, could be taken the wrong way if you have a dirty mind (if you're still making her a servant of Carnala). I'll even translate it for you, I just have to pull up my dictionary again. I also mentioned the Gishtahu auspice earlier; you can find it on page 193 or 194 of <i>Signs of the Moon</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to call her <b>Blood-Mane</b>, becuase of her redhead and fur, but <b>Cunning Tongue</b> is probably better one. Will look on Gishtahu.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T17:57:42-07:00","id":128655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127028-ex-bale-hound-mentor?p=128653#post128653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Game is set in mountains valley, but wolves and bears fur trade post could be good one for this, yes? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I was going to call her <b>Blood-Mane</b>, becuase of her redhead and fur, but <b>Cunning Tongue</b> is probably better one. Will look on Gishtahu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood-Mane is also a good one for a Gishtahu. She could also pass as a really nasty Rahu if she had something that could change the look of her moon-brands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T23:24:20-07:00","id":128776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127028-ex-bale-hound-mentor?p=128655#post128655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood-Mane is also a good one for a Gishtahu. She could also pass as a really nasty Rahu if she had something that could change the look of her moon-brands.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see this for Blood Moon Auspice, but I don't think it's good fit for her. She isn't canibalistic ( it would be Hound of Gluttony reather ), she isn't &quot;evil because of star-crossed curse&quot;. I don't see her as martyr figure. She is wicked because she likes it. She manipulate people because it's fun. But also she isn't totally depraved monster that rest of Bale Hounds are - she just likes to make &quot;pranks&quot;. And this pranks could be miming man deep in the woods with promise of taking her body - and then leaving them on surly death there. <br /> <br /> She doesn't feel Cathalith for me, as the don't looking for Glory, only wicked satisfaction in manipulating others. Thinking more about primary Renown for her, I would connect her with Cunning of Irraka - she want to test herself and others in battle of minds and playing with lives of other. PCs are pawns in her play, and she will use them to battle they old adversaries, even if they don't know whole truth why they do it.<br /> <br /> I think &quot;calculating&quot; Irraka would most suitable Auspice for her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T00:19:09-07:00","id":128792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127028-ex-bale-hound-mentor?p=128776#post128776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see this for Blood Moon Auspice, but I don't think it's good fit for her. She isn't canibalistic ( it would be Hound of Gluttony reather ), she isn't &quot;evil because of star-crossed curse&quot;. I don't see her as martyr figure. She is wicked because she likes it. She manipulate people because it's fun. But also she isn't totally depraved monster that rest of Bale Hounds are - she just likes to make &quot;pranks&quot;. And this pranks could be miming man deep in the woods with promise of taking her body - and then leaving them on surly death there.<br /> <br /> She doesn't feel Cathalith for me, as the don't looking for Glory, only wicked satisfaction in manipulating others. Thinking more about primary Renown for her, I would connect her with Cunning of Irraka - she want to test herself and others in battle of minds and playing with lives of other. PCs are pawns in her play, and she will use them to battle they old adversaries, even if they don't know whole truth why they do it.<br /> <br /> I think &quot;calculating&quot; Irraka would most suitable Auspice for her.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, her First Tongue name would be <b>Gakaleme</b>. It means &quot;Cunning Tongue&quot; with the implication that she was born with an inherent ability to be a cunning little witch; the lack of a hyphen or a space indicates that it is in her very nature, believed to be a fundamental part of her being, according to the syntax rules I've observed in FT (though the devs can always rebuke me on this). If you wanted, you could also spell it <b>Gakal-Eme</b>, with the idea that the cunning part of her is a piece of who she is, but not something that is fundamentally part of her basic psychological/spiritual build.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}